# Vonos — Environment Variables (local development)

Copy to `.env` at repo root and/or per-app as needed.

For staging/beta and production, see:
  docs/ENVIRONMENTS.md
  .env.staging.example
  .env.production.example

```bash
# Web (apps/web) — copy to apps/web/.env.local
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
# No trailing slash — gooberrandall prod: https://api-production-a4a1.up.railway.app
# (legacy Zyhvar URL: https://vonos-backend-production.up.railway.app — do not use)
# Set to `true` only to bypass login during UI-only work
NEXT_PUBLIC_SKIP_AUTH=false

# API (apps/api)
# Neon: use the *-pooler* host. Prisma auto-adds pgbouncer=true + connection_limit.
# Multi-user: 15 per API process is a solid default on Neon Launch/Scale (pooler).
# Local Postgres can go higher. Do not multiply blindly across many Railway replicas.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://vonos:vonos@localhost:5432/vonos
# Neon example:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASS@ep-xxx-pooler.eu-west-2.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
PRISMA_CONNECTION_LIMIT=15
PRISMA_POOL_TIMEOUT=60
JWT_SECRET=change-me-in-production
JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRES=3h
JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRES=7d
# Optional: HMAC secret for public invoice share links (`/invoice/:token`). Falls back to JWT_SECRET.
INVOICE_SHARE_SECRET=
WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
# Comma-separated allowed frontend origins for CORS (also merges with defaults).
# Example: WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000,https://vonosgroup.com,https://www.vonosgroup.com,https://app.vonosautos.com
# Refresh cookie SameSite: omit for auto (production → none for Vercel↔Railway; local → lax).
# Force with COOKIE_SAMESITE=none|lax when web and API are on different sites in staging.
# COOKIE_SAMESITE=none
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3001
# Set true to log every Prisma SQL + duration (local/staging audit only)
PRISMA_LOG_QUERIES=false
# Upstash Redis — REQUIRED for staging/prod. Without these, report/dashboard
# caches use in-memory fallback and reset on every deploy / multi-instance miss.
# Create a free DB at https://console.upstash.com → copy REST URL + token.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Public parts shop (Paystack) — sandbox keys until KYC is live
PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=
# Optional override; defaults to https://api.paystack.co
# PAYSTACK_PAYMENT_URL=https://api.paystack.co

# WhatsApp customer status notifies (job stage → owner phone + /track link)
# Public site origin for track URLs (defaults to first WEB_ORIGIN)
# PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.vonosgroup.com
# Meta WhatsApp Cloud API — without these, staff get a wa.me deep link instead
# WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
# WHATSAPP_API_VERSION=v21.0
# Approved template for outbound notifies (body: name, plate, status, track URL)
# WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_NAME=job_status_update
# WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_LANG=en
# Auto-notify on job status advance (default on). Set false to require the UI checkbox only.
# WHATSAPP_AUTO_NOTIFY=true
```

Start Postgres locally:

```bash
docker compose up -d
```
